<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dutch Rabobank opens SAfrica representative office.</title>
<headline>Dutch Rabobank opens SAfrica representative office.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Economic Affairs Minister Hans Wijers will officially open Rabobank's southern Africa representative office in Johannesburg on Tuesday during the state visit of Queen Beatrix to South Africa.</p>
<p>The bank said the new office will service South Africa, Zimbabwe, Botswana and Namibia, focussing on food and agricultural business.</p>
<p>Dr Henk Visser, member of the executive board of Rabobank Netherlands, said he believed this sector, which already plays an important role in Southern African economies, offered good prospects for the future.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
